  "actual_construction": [
    "Choose an actual positive component from the reference profile, then a closed nonempty interval strictly inside its B.normalizationLeft/Right interval.",
    "The actual scalar source is g(r) = -deriv (spacesLeftCutoff l u) r, independently of angle. Its compact support lies in that interval and its physical integral equals one by the existing radial integral identity and the fundamental theorem of calculus.",
    "Use surjectivity of the original IsSobolevModel at exponent 3/4 to encode this exact radial function in the original height space.",
    "Replace only PhysicalSpacesData.psi. Retain height, circle, chiLeft and the original continuous compatibility functional Q.",
    "Identify Q with the existing spacesSourceFunctional using its actual physical integral equation, then obtain the new continuous rank-one projection from spaces_source_projection with tame loss zero and base two.",
    "Repackage C, R, L and K by copying every field. The state/source spaces, gradings, state sector, parameter neighborhood, all actual maps and the Through03 predicates are definitionally unchanged after these copies.",
    "Retain all fourteen CanonicalGeometry fields. Prove the actual AuxiliaryColumnGauge of the new chosen column from its global radial identity and its support in K.normalizationRegion=B.region."
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "This is an existential replacement of the auxiliary column. It does not assert that the arbitrary old S.psi was radial.",
    "The new normalizer is encoded in the same original height model; no altered source functional or replacement profile/geometry witness is used.",
    "The ReferenceJets and CurrentJets clauses involving the auxiliary atom are not claimed preserved, because that actual source changes. They need their own bounds for the constructed compact radial column.",
    "No final PrimitiveGeometryProperties or complete nonlinear existence theorem is assumed as an input or claimed as proved.",
    "The sources are held drafts; static checks do not constitute Lean compilation or a CI success."
  ],
